(2) Police Officers travelling under Regulation 16 of
Chap. 23:50 are not entitled to payment of Upkeep Allowance.
24. (1) “Upkeep Allowance” refers to a specified sum of money
paid to a Travelling Officer each month to assist in the main-
tenance and repairs of his private motor vehicle authorised for
use in the performance of his official duty.
(2) Upkeep Allowance shall also be paid in the following
circumstances:
(a) on ordinary sick leave;
(b) where an officer is on sick leave followed by
extended sick leave during any month—for the whole
of that month only;
(c) on occasions of casual absences;
(d) during periods of annual leave earned and
accumulated under the Police Service Regulations;
(e) for the first three months in respect of full pay study
leave not exceeding twelve months (the allowance is
not payable for any part where the period of study
leave exceeds twelve months);
(f) where an officer travels abroad on official duty;
(g) during periods of special duty leave up to fourteen
(14) days;
(h) where an officer has been suspended from duty
without loss of pay;
